From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: take override-redirect from MapNotify

Wine creates a toplevel as override-redirect and flips it to managed with
XChangeWindowAttributes while it is unmapped, which generates no X event.
When add_win reads the attributes before the flip, the window stays cached
as override-redirect and is left out of GAMESCOPE_FOCUSABLE_APPS. Steam
then keeps its loading screen over the game, as with A Plague Tale:
Innocence (752590). Before 2238420d, the focus nudge's move usually
refreshed the flag.

MapNotify carries the current override-redirect state, so refresh the
cached flag there rather than re-reading the attributes.

Closes: #2457
---
 src/steamcompmgr.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index f00b62c..cb3b9c6 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -8778,7 +8778,11 @@ void xwayland_ctx_t::Dispatch()
 				steamcompmgr_win_t * w = find_win(ctx, ev.xmap.window);
 
 				if (w && w->xwayland().id == ev.xmap.window)
+				{
+					// Wine flips override-redirect while unmapped and the flip itself sends no event.
+					w->xwayland().a.override_redirect = ev.xmap.override_redirect;
 					map_win(ctx, ev.xmap.window, ev.xmap.serial);
+				}
 				break;
 			}
 			case UnmapNotify:
